@startuml
title P1 Telegram Adapter, History and Presence - Component Boundaries

left to right direction
skinparam componentStyle rectangle

actor "Telegram User" as TgUser
actor "Pulsar App" as App

rectangle "STORY-260712-34kbkn\nTelegram parity + history/presence" {
  [Telegram Transport\nvoice/audio/callback updates] as TgTransport
  [Inline Action Router\nlegacy default + action callbacks] as InlineRouter
  [Delivery Presentation Model\nhuman labels + receipt wording] as Presentation
  [Presence Surface\nsanitized presence + DND/block] as Presence
  [History/Receipt Query\nrecent transmissions + aggregates] as History
}

rectangle "STORY-260712-2ve1c8\nIdentity + ActorContext" as Identity
rectangle "STORY-260712-ld674h\nSubmitMedia + legacy voice bridge" as Ingest
rectangle "STORY-260712-25lysg\nCreateTransmission + receipts + DND semantics" as Tx
rectangle "STORY-260712-2e36uz\nWindows/macOS UI integration" as UI

TgUser --> TgTransport
TgTransport --> Identity : authorize actor
TgTransport --> Ingest : submit voice/audio
TgTransport --> InlineRouter : callback events

InlineRouter --> Tx : create transmission\nor legacy after_current
InlineRouter --> Presentation

Tx --> History : transmission + target states
Tx --> Presence : target capability\nDND/block result

Identity --> Presentation : actor + orbit labels
Presentation --> History
Presentation --> Presence

App --> History
App --> Presence
History --> UI
Presence --> UI

note bottom
  This story owns presentation-oriented parity:
  human names, routing labels, presence sanitization,
  Telegram inline actions, and history/receipt read models.
  It does not own SubmitMedia internals or transmission scheduling semantics.
end note

@enduml
